1
00:00:14,714 --> 00:00:16,950
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

2
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:19,352
Sayaka! Stop!

3
00:00:19,419 --> 00:00:20,520
Keep it down!

4
00:00:22,555 --> 00:00:24,991
Hey! Watch out!

5
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:33,233
Hey, old lady! Why did you do that?

6
00:00:33,299 --> 00:00:36,603
- "Old lady"?
- Why did you do that, old lady?

7
00:00:36,669 --> 00:00:38,471
Hurry up and fix it!

8
00:00:38,605 --> 00:00:41,107
It's your fault for doing this right here!

9
00:00:41,174 --> 00:00:43,610
I'm sorry! Okay, everyone.
Let's do this over there.

10
00:00:43,676 --> 00:00:44,878
Move this stuff!

11
00:00:44,944 --> 00:00:46,579
Let's clean up!
Let's see who's fastest! Go!

12
00:00:46,646 --> 00:00:48,882
- How dare you call me "old lady."
- So what?

13
00:01:02,262 --> 00:01:04,264
Mr. Nishiki. We've been expecting you.

14
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:05,398
We've been expecting you.

15
00:01:05,465 --> 00:01:07,333
NISHIKI GROUP CEO
TOSHIRO NISHIKI

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,234
Here you are.

17
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:20,080
Is this good enough?

18
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:33,693
Sorry, everyone.

19
00:01:35,628 --> 00:01:38,498
Hey, old man! Why did you do that?

20
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:40,366
- Do you have any idea who I am?
- Who are you?

21
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:41,534
Dr. Daimon!

22
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,069
SURGEON
KIMIHIKO MURASAKI

23
00:01:43,136 --> 00:01:44,737
"Doctor"?

24
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:50,076
You're telling me
this rude woman is a doctor?

25
00:01:50,243 --> 00:01:52,912
- She's just a part-timer.
- A part-timer?

26
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,515
Is this hospital all right?

27
00:01:55,582 --> 00:01:56,816
Who are you calling rude?

28
00:01:56,883 --> 00:01:59,119
Put back the dominoes you knocked over.

29
00:02:00,653 --> 00:02:01,855
Now.

30
00:02:02,422 --> 00:02:04,090
I'm terribly sorry about this.

31
00:02:04,557 --> 00:02:06,960
She is truly
an unbelievably rude part-timer.

32
00:02:07,393 --> 00:02:08,428
Let's go.

33
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:11,498
Hey!

34
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,802
Hey! You!

35
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,403
Darn you!

36
00:02:18,872 --> 00:02:20,507
Okay, let's set them up again.

37
00:02:21,841 --> 00:02:24,744
KENJI KOSAWA

38
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:27,013
You're really fast, mister.

39
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:33,586
- Mister?
- Mister?

40
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,122
- Are you okay?
- Out of the way!

41
00:02:36,189 --> 00:02:38,158
- Mister!
- I'm going to touch here.

42
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:40,093
- Mister! Are you okay?
- Mister.

43
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,428
- Get a stretcher, now!
- Okay!

44
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:45,398
NURSE
MASAKO OHMA

45
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:50,170
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

46
00:02:52,438 --> 00:02:56,676
Rapid pulse. Conjunctival pallor.
Dull pain in the right abdomen.

47
00:02:56,743 --> 00:02:58,711
- Let's get a CT scan.
- Right.

48
00:02:58,778 --> 00:03:02,081
This is Mr. Kosawa from room 403.
He was just released today.

49
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:05,485
What? That's insane.

50
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:06,886
I'm sorry.

51
00:03:07,887 --> 00:03:12,325
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

52
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:17,030
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

53
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:19,732
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

54
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:23,536
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

55
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:25,071
ACTING HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
NICHOLAS TANGE

56
00:03:27,273 --> 00:03:28,441
Excuse me.

57
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:32,712
Toshiro Nishiki, CEO of
the Nishiki Group, has just checked in.

58
00:03:32,812 --> 00:03:35,148
I see.
The man referred by Director Hiruma.

59
00:03:35,648 --> 00:03:41,387
He's hoping to get a transplant to treat
his hereditary ATTR amyloidosis, right?

60
00:03:41,454 --> 00:03:44,591
That's right.
He has promised to invest one billion

61
00:03:44,791 --> 00:03:49,162
into the fund we need investors for
if his surgery succeeds.

62
00:03:55,301 --> 00:03:56,536
Awesome!

63
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:07,447
I am the acting hospital director,
Mr. Tange.

64
00:04:07,981 --> 00:04:11,150
Why hasn't Director Hiruma come to see me?

65
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:13,119
I'm terribly sorry.

66
00:04:13,286 --> 00:04:17,323
The director is currently in jail,
under investigation.

67
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:19,726
Is this hospital all right?

68
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:23,496
- I don't know.
- Not to worry.

69
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,432
A team especially for you

70
00:04:26,666 --> 00:04:30,103
will be chosen from Totei University
Hospital's best medical staff

71
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:34,007
to handle your treatment.
How are you feeling now?

72
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:35,808
Incredibly bad!

73
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:44,083
But there's no way
I'm going to retire yet.

74
00:04:47,754 --> 00:04:50,757
My life is worth 500 billion yen!

75
00:04:50,923 --> 00:04:53,226
That precious
500-billion-yen body of yours,

76
00:04:54,761 --> 00:04:57,397
please entrust it to us.

77
00:05:00,566 --> 00:05:03,503
I heard about your desire to invest.

78
00:05:04,837 --> 00:05:10,243
We will give you
the finest treatment possible.

79
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:13,913
Go ahead.

80
00:05:22,355 --> 00:05:26,759
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance
maverick doctor, who was never part of</i>

81
00:05:27,026 --> 00:05:30,763
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

82
00:05:31,631 --> 00:05:34,634
- I'm returning this patient.
- Oh, welcome back!

83
00:05:34,801 --> 00:05:37,337
- You can come back?
- Yes, unfortunately.

84
00:05:37,403 --> 00:05:41,240
If you're still sick, how could they
kick you out just because you're broke?

85
00:05:41,307 --> 00:05:43,009
That's what a hospital does.

86
00:05:43,943 --> 00:05:48,214
Once the poor are cured,
they get out right away.

87
00:05:48,281 --> 00:05:50,583
Dr. Daimon!

88
00:05:51,284 --> 00:05:53,986
- Daimon! Good morning!
- You look frightening!

89
00:05:54,654 --> 00:06:00,727
- Let's go.
<i>- This woman hates groups, authority,</i>

90
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,595
<i>and restrictions.</i>

91
00:06:02,929 --> 00:06:06,366
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

92
00:06:06,432 --> 00:06:07,500
<i>are her weapons.</i>

93
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:09,969
PRIVATE ROOM C

94
00:06:13,239 --> 00:06:16,142
Find possible donors among
CEO Nishiki's relatives right away.

95
00:06:16,275 --> 00:06:17,343
Got it.

96
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:25,485
Oh, good morning, Dr. Daimon.

97
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,989
Hey! The least you can do is say hello!

98
00:06:30,456 --> 00:06:32,892
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

99
00:06:33,292 --> 00:06:36,529
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

100
00:06:47,473 --> 00:06:48,541
Case 12.

101
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:52,779
This is our most urgent patient.

102
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:56,516
Toshiro Nishiki, male, age 60.

103
00:06:56,883 --> 00:07:01,354
He's diagnosed with
hereditary ATTR amyloidosis,

104
00:07:02,121 --> 00:07:05,224
late onset V30M variant.

105
00:07:06,025 --> 00:07:07,827
Due to peripheral nerve disorder,

106
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,796
he suffers pain and numbness in his legs.

107
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:13,966
He can lose consciousness due to
nausea and orthostatic hypotension.

108
00:07:14,233 --> 00:07:16,569
This serious disease is a genetic mutation

109
00:07:16,669 --> 00:07:19,839
that manifests in amyloid deposits
caused by abnormal proteins.

110
00:07:20,139 --> 00:07:23,776
Over 95 percent of those proteins
are created in the liver.

111
00:07:24,177 --> 00:07:28,147
The current treatment is
injection of tafamidis

112
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:30,383
to relieve the symptoms.

113
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:33,686
- Why?
- What do you mean "why"?

114
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:36,122
It's the first medication in the world

115
00:07:36,189 --> 00:07:38,357
that has been approved for this disease.

116
00:07:38,491 --> 00:07:41,160
I'm asking
why don't we perform a transplant?

117
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,562
Let me do it!

118
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:45,264
We're discussing this because
we can't get a donor so fast.

119
00:07:45,331 --> 00:07:48,901
- Like I said, why?
- Because we haven't found a donor.

120
00:07:49,001 --> 00:07:50,169
What about his family?

121
00:07:50,536 --> 00:07:53,906
There must be one relative
willing to offer a healthy liver.

122
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,542
I've met with Mr. Nishiki's family.

123
00:07:56,609 --> 00:07:57,877
However...

124
00:07:58,010 --> 00:08:02,782
Mr. Nishiki needs a liver transplant.
Won't any of you donate?

125
00:08:03,549 --> 00:08:05,251
What about you, Mrs. Nishiki?

126
00:08:05,585 --> 00:08:07,920
What? Me?

127
00:08:08,688 --> 00:08:11,691
Come here for a second.

128
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:15,361
Why do I have to let my liver
get all carved up

129
00:08:15,895 --> 00:08:20,766
for that cheating husband of mine?

130
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:24,003
I see. And you? You're his eldest.

131
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:26,672
There's no way I'm doing that.
I don't consider him my father.

132
00:08:26,739 --> 00:08:29,375
- But--
- He's bossy and short-tempered.

133
00:08:29,442 --> 00:08:32,512
He's beaten me
more than once or twice you know.

134
00:08:33,479 --> 00:08:34,881
What about the second son?

135
00:08:34,947 --> 00:08:39,552
I wouldn't do it for 100 million.
Everyone here hopes he dies soon.

136
00:08:39,619 --> 00:08:42,355
<i>Not a single one of them
gave their approval.</i>

137
00:08:42,722 --> 00:08:44,957
- That's so awful.
- Yes, it is.

138
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:47,793
Without a donor, I can't operate!

139
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:52,865
Are you only concerned about
whether you're able to operate or not?

140
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:59,338
TOTEI

141
00:08:59,405 --> 00:09:01,274
Aren't there any other relatives?

142
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:05,511
He's such a womanizer
that his own wife hates him, right?

143
00:09:06,145 --> 00:09:09,649
Then he must have one or two
illegitimate children.

144
00:09:10,082 --> 00:09:11,684
I didn't look that far.

145
00:09:11,751 --> 00:09:16,522
There is one more. His youngest daughter.

146
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:18,991
What? How did you know that, Tako?

147
00:09:19,659 --> 00:09:21,594
Kaji! Ask that girl right away!

148
00:09:22,161 --> 00:09:23,863
Don't order your boss around!

149
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,331
- Oh, right.
- Ebina!

150
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:26,566
Sorry. My mistake.

151
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:31,804
Well, she ran away and her family
doesn't know where she is.

152
00:09:31,871 --> 00:09:33,205
She's missing?

153
00:09:35,608 --> 00:09:37,243
This is a problem.

154
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:40,179
If that's the case,
then our only choice is

155
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:45,318
to hospitalize him and treat him for
his peripheral nerve disorder.

156
00:09:46,018 --> 00:09:48,387
Please do that, Dr. Hamachi.

157
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:49,822
Leave it to me.

158
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:51,157
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

159
00:09:51,657 --> 00:09:56,896
The surgical transplant team
will continue to explain to his family

160
00:09:57,396 --> 00:10:00,466
and find a donor as soon as possible.

161
00:10:00,666 --> 00:10:01,734
Yes, sir!

162
00:10:04,203 --> 00:10:05,538
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

163
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:09,308
That is all for this conference.

164
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,010
Hold on a second!

165
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,513
We haven't finished
discussing this patient.

166
00:10:20,219 --> 00:10:21,287
Who is this patient?

167
00:10:21,354 --> 00:10:24,423
He's a stage three liver cancer patient
who left on his own.

168
00:10:24,824 --> 00:10:27,193
Dr. Daimon brought him back.

169
00:10:27,259 --> 00:10:30,529
He would die if we released him as-is.

170
00:10:30,596 --> 00:10:33,899
All the beds in the large rooms are full.

171
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:38,871
Also, Dr. Tako determined he could be
treated as an outpatient.

172
00:10:40,606 --> 00:10:43,442
This is quite different than
our handling of that rich old guy.

173
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:47,546
Are you abandoning the poor patients
in the group infirmary?

174
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:53,419
Of course not. The value of
every patient's life is the same.

175
00:10:53,886 --> 00:10:55,655
They're more valuable than
the earth itself.

176
00:10:57,823 --> 00:11:02,228
Why don't I place that patient
under your care, Dr. Daimon?

177
00:11:03,129 --> 00:11:06,866
Then if we find a donor,
I'll perform the surgery.

178
00:11:06,966 --> 00:11:10,903
Of course. Okay, Dr. Daimon.

179
00:11:12,071 --> 00:11:13,239
Okay, Nichotan.

180
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,553
KOSAWA'S GIRLFRIEND
YURI

181
00:11:32,391 --> 00:11:35,528
Daimon, how do you open
these digital medical charts?

182
00:11:35,594 --> 00:11:39,031
I always had the assistants do this,
so I don't know how.

183
00:11:39,665 --> 00:11:43,102
Oh, no! I sent an email!
How am I supposed to do this?

184
00:11:43,469 --> 00:11:46,105
- Leave me alone!
- Darn you! Hey.

185
00:11:46,272 --> 00:11:48,140
- How do you open digital charts?
- Hey.

186
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,711
Wasn't Kenji Kosawa
originally your patient?

187
00:11:51,811 --> 00:11:53,479
Yes, that's right.

188
00:11:54,113 --> 00:11:57,883
"Outpatient treatment possible."
Are you stupid, Tako?

189
00:11:57,950 --> 00:11:59,852
Hey! Director! That's power harassment!

190
00:11:59,919 --> 00:12:02,755
Hey! Who said the freelancer
could harass people?

191
00:12:02,822 --> 00:12:05,491
She'd never listen if I said that.
Deal with it yourself.

192
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:07,993
Tell me everything
you haven't written in the record.

193
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:12,798
I didn't want to abandon him either!

194
00:12:13,199 --> 00:12:14,767
He's a childhood friend of mine.

195
00:12:15,334 --> 00:12:16,869
A childhood friend?

196
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:22,641
He has no family,
so finding a donor isn't easy.

197
00:12:23,809 --> 00:12:26,512
Chemotherapy hasn't had any effect,

198
00:12:26,612 --> 00:12:29,548
and his hepatic reserve is so bad,
we can't operate on his liver.

199
00:12:30,316 --> 00:12:32,818
Our only choice is a liver transplant.

200
00:12:32,952 --> 00:12:35,287
He was hospitalized, waiting for a donor,

201
00:12:35,354 --> 00:12:36,322
but...

202
00:12:36,655 --> 00:12:40,326
<i>he hasn't paid his hospital bills
and he's taking up space.</i>

203
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,862
<i>So the admin told me
to urge him to check out.</i>

204
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:48,367
How about checking out
and switching to outpatient care?

205
00:12:49,468 --> 00:12:50,436
What?

206
00:12:50,903 --> 00:12:52,638
That's what I told him.

207
00:12:53,205 --> 00:12:56,809
Tako, how can you
call yourself his friend?

208
00:12:57,476 --> 00:12:59,712
- What?
- Do you know what it feels like

209
00:12:59,979 --> 00:13:02,148
to have a hospital abandon you?

210
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,651
Do you know what it feels like
to have nowhere to go?

211
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:07,353
- Yes.
- No, you don't.

212
00:13:07,419 --> 00:13:12,525
Excuse me. Dr. Ebina,
Tako hasn't done anything wrong.

213
00:13:12,591 --> 00:13:14,360
- Do you know what it's like, Hara?
- No, I don't.

214
00:13:15,094 --> 00:13:18,330
- What about you, Daimon?
- What? You look frightening.

215
00:13:19,231 --> 00:13:21,600
- What the heck is with you?
- You don't get it.

216
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:22,902
Tako.

217
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:24,737
Would you just get out of here?

218
00:13:25,237 --> 00:13:27,406
Don't talk like that. It's power play.

219
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:31,443
What are you doing, Mr. Kosawa?
Please get back in bed.

220
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:33,445
Mr. Kosawa!

221
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:36,282
Wait, Ken! Don't push yourself like this.

222
00:13:36,348 --> 00:13:38,250
I can't cause any more trouble
for the hospital.

223
00:13:38,784 --> 00:13:39,852
Hey! Wait!

224
00:13:39,919 --> 00:13:42,054
You'll collapse again if you leave now.

225
00:13:43,055 --> 00:13:44,456
Dr. Daimon.

226
00:13:44,924 --> 00:13:47,259
Oh, are you Dr. Daimon?

227
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:49,695
I heard you saved Ken.

228
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:52,431
- Thank you.
- It was nothing.

229
00:13:52,598 --> 00:13:54,266
I still haven't saved him.

230
00:13:56,468 --> 00:13:57,770
- Wait.
- I'm fine.

231
00:13:57,837 --> 00:14:00,339
Say, are you his girlfriend?

232
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:01,874
Yes.

233
00:14:01,941 --> 00:14:04,009
Then hurry up and get married.

234
00:14:04,076 --> 00:14:05,978
As his wife, you can give him your liver.

235
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:13,652
Sorry. This doctor is a little odd.

236
00:14:15,054 --> 00:14:16,388
Dr. Daimon.

237
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:19,658
We can't get married.

238
00:14:20,392 --> 00:14:21,360
Why not?

239
00:14:22,628 --> 00:14:25,231
Her father says he'd never approve.

240
00:14:25,965 --> 00:14:29,201
It's only natural.
I hardly make any money,

241
00:14:29,401 --> 00:14:31,170
and on top of that, I'm sick.

242
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:33,272
I can't even pay my hospital bills.

243
00:14:34,406 --> 00:14:38,477
But even if everyone in the world
were against it,

244
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,979
I still want to marry Ken.

245
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:43,349
Yuri. I want to marry you after I'm cured

246
00:14:43,782 --> 00:14:45,951
and able to gain your father's approval.

247
00:14:47,953 --> 00:14:49,088
Ken.

248
00:14:49,455 --> 00:14:51,657
- What a lot of trouble.
- What?

249
00:14:52,024 --> 00:14:55,961
I just want to operate.
I won't let you leave until then.

250
00:14:56,028 --> 00:14:58,130
Hey! Dr. Daimon!

251
00:15:00,866 --> 00:15:05,337
Dr. Daimon, please give my liver to Ken!

252
00:15:05,604 --> 00:15:06,906
Please!

253
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:09,808
Use my liver for his liver transplant.

254
00:15:09,875 --> 00:15:13,279
- Impossible.
- How come?

255
00:15:13,545 --> 00:15:17,917
In Japan, living organ transplants
between strangers are not approved.

256
00:15:20,185 --> 00:15:22,221
Your love won't save Ken.

257
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:26,225
The only thing that can save him
is the liver of a qualified donor.

258
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:32,264
Today, we're going to administer
a laser Doppler test.

259
00:15:32,531 --> 00:15:35,734
You give me nothing but tests!
When can I get a transplant?

260
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:39,138
Hey!

261
00:15:40,472 --> 00:15:43,509
You again? You dumb part-timer!

262
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:47,379
- Is this hospital all right?
- So have you found a donor?

263
00:15:49,348 --> 00:15:52,751
I didn't think so.
Let me operate when you do.

264
00:15:52,818 --> 00:15:55,120
Even as a part-timer,
I'm better than these guys.

265
00:15:55,521 --> 00:15:58,991
- Who do you think you are?
- I am terribly sorry.

266
00:15:59,091 --> 00:16:00,526
Let's go.

267
00:16:04,763 --> 00:16:09,201
Dr. Daimon, the acting director
wants to have lunch with you.

268
00:16:10,069 --> 00:16:11,136
Why?

269
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:20,312
She hates romance and marriage,
and her only purpose in life is surgery?

270
00:16:20,379 --> 00:16:22,514
What's wrong with Dr. Daimon?

271
00:16:22,581 --> 00:16:26,785
She's uninterested in living males
and only loves organs.

272
00:16:26,852 --> 00:16:28,287
What's wrong, Tako?

273
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:31,156
I want to help Kosawa and his girlfriend.

274
00:16:32,091 --> 00:16:34,793
But he does dream of bringing happiness

275
00:16:34,927 --> 00:16:36,862
to the people of the world
through dominoes.

276
00:16:37,363 --> 00:16:38,497
Dominoes?

277
00:16:39,465 --> 00:16:40,666
This is him.

278
00:16:41,567 --> 00:16:44,837
- You can be a domino master?
- Yes.

279
00:16:44,903 --> 00:16:46,171
Looks like fun.

280
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:48,540
Maybe I'll quit being a doctor
and be a domino master.

281
00:16:48,607 --> 00:16:50,743
- What's your problem, Dr. Ebina?
- That would be better.

282
00:16:50,876 --> 00:16:51,977
You like that?

283
00:16:52,277 --> 00:16:53,812
Can you make a living as a domino master?

284
00:16:53,879 --> 00:16:55,981
It sure isn't easy.

285
00:16:56,382 --> 00:16:58,484
But if Kosawa married his girlfriend,

286
00:16:58,550 --> 00:17:00,619
it would be
the ultimate reverse gold digger.

287
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:02,988
But he's not that kind of guy.

288
00:17:03,055 --> 00:17:05,324
- "Ultimate reverse gold digger"?
- "Ultimate reverse gold digger"?

289
00:17:08,961 --> 00:17:10,129
Sorry.

290
00:17:11,230 --> 00:17:12,898
Wait. Hold on a second.

291
00:17:14,833 --> 00:17:18,437
I stewed this feijoada
all night last night.

292
00:17:19,104 --> 00:17:20,239
I see.

293
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:23,542
SECRETARY TO THE ACTING HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RURI IKURA

294
00:17:23,609 --> 00:17:25,711
- That's delicious.
- I'm glad you like it.

295
00:17:26,078 --> 00:17:29,915
To reduce costs, the acting director
makes his own lunch every day.

296
00:17:31,183 --> 00:17:34,153
After I arrived, I was astonished
at just how horrendous

297
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,155
the financial situation is here.

298
00:17:36,355 --> 00:17:40,793
If this main hospital falls,
the satellites will fall like dominoes.

299
00:17:41,326 --> 00:17:43,362
Many patients will be cast
into the streets

300
00:17:43,429 --> 00:17:46,865
and numerous patients will never be saved.

301
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:52,037
The reforms I'm making now, Dr. Daimon,

302
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:55,007
I believe you can understand.

303
00:17:59,945 --> 00:18:03,248
Excuse me, but are you listening to
what the acting director is saying?

304
00:18:06,552 --> 00:18:07,786
Dr. Daimon.

305
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,457
That was delicious.

306
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:17,663
Japan has the great saying,
"Eating out of the same pot."

307
00:18:18,363 --> 00:18:22,134
Dr. Daimon, as a partner
in these operational reforms,

308
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:25,003
I can count on you
to fight alongside me, right?

309
00:18:26,672 --> 00:18:29,408
Making tons of money from wealthy patients

310
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:31,643
while kicking the poor
out of the hospital.

311
00:18:31,844 --> 00:18:33,545
That's your real intention,
right, Nichotan?

312
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:36,148
- Dr. Daimon!
- If I don't do that,

313
00:18:36,315 --> 00:18:38,550
I cannot save this hospital
that's on the verge of death.

314
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,587
The feijoada
and <i>pao de queijo</i> were fantastic.

315
00:18:42,988 --> 00:18:45,457
Thank you for the meal.

316
00:18:45,757 --> 00:18:47,993
My friend, let us talk a while longer.

317
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:49,495
I decline.

318
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,298
Even if we do eat from the same pot,

319
00:18:53,365 --> 00:18:54,900
it doesn't mean we hang out together.

320
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,536
Excuse me, Assistant Hospital Director.

321
00:19:00,272 --> 00:19:03,208
Assistant Hospital Director, I think
we've found a donor for CEO Nishiki.

322
00:19:03,275 --> 00:19:04,309
You have?

323
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:06,545
We found the missing daughter.

324
00:19:06,612 --> 00:19:10,382
Yuri Nishiki. She's visiting her
boyfriend in this hospital today.

325
00:19:10,449 --> 00:19:12,417
Is she that girlfriend?

326
00:19:12,851 --> 00:19:14,453
Actually, yes.

327
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:17,322
Why didn't you tell me that sooner, Tako?

328
00:19:17,389 --> 00:19:20,392
- That's power harassment!
- They told me not to!

329
00:19:20,759 --> 00:19:22,127
She doesn't want anyone to know

330
00:19:22,194 --> 00:19:23,762
she's the daughter of
the Nishiki Group CEO.

331
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:26,598
Do whatever it takes
to get her to be the donor.

332
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:29,468
I don't think that will be possible.

333
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:33,071
She despises her father, so she ran away.

334
00:19:33,138 --> 00:19:35,974
Do everything you can
to get her to approve.

335
00:19:36,475 --> 00:19:37,609
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

336
00:19:37,709 --> 00:19:39,811
- Where's your "Yes, sir"?
- That's power harassment!

337
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:43,081
I told you to tell me everything
that wasn't on the record, Tako!

338
00:19:43,148 --> 00:19:43,982
Cut that out!

339
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:46,318
Don't worry about money anymore.

340
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:50,289
I'll work hard to save for your operation.

341
00:19:50,756 --> 00:19:52,791
I can't make you do all that.

342
00:19:53,325 --> 00:19:56,361
It's all right.
You do your best to fight too.

343
00:20:02,501 --> 00:20:04,636
Are you still with that guy, Yuri?

344
00:20:05,604 --> 00:20:06,572
Father...

345
00:20:07,673 --> 00:20:09,174
- Well...
- I'm sorry.

346
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:11,376
Don't criticize Yuri.

347
00:20:11,443 --> 00:20:12,878
Are you hospitalized here?

348
00:20:13,545 --> 00:20:14,413
Yes.

349
00:20:14,479 --> 00:20:18,784
No matter what you say, Father,
I will stay with Kenji.

350
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:20,819
I need Ken!

351
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,054
Why you...

352
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:24,323
Mr. Nishiki, you'll hurt yourself!

353
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,726
What a disaster!

354
00:20:27,926 --> 00:20:31,630
What's the point in letting people,
who produce nothing, live?

355
00:20:32,698 --> 00:20:35,667
Father, how can you say that?

356
00:20:35,801 --> 00:20:37,369
- That's so cruel!
- Stop it, Yuri.

357
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:44,543
Ken?

358
00:20:45,377 --> 00:20:46,445
Ken!

359
00:20:48,046 --> 00:20:49,681
Doctor, it's Ken!

360
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:51,950
- Kenji?
- Ken!

361
00:20:52,050 --> 00:20:53,785
Kenji! Are you all right?

362
00:20:53,885 --> 00:20:56,355
Possible internal hemorrhage
from the tumor. Stretcher!

363
00:20:56,588 --> 00:20:57,823
Right away!

364
00:20:57,923 --> 00:20:59,791
Ken, pull yourself together!

365
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:02,127
- Get it now!
- I am!

366
00:21:16,341 --> 00:21:17,476
Ken.

367
00:21:27,552 --> 00:21:30,656
You're Yuri Nishiki, right?
Can I talk to you for a moment?

368
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,190
Okay.

369
00:21:32,257 --> 00:21:34,893
It's about your father
who's hospitalized here.

370
00:22:16,368 --> 00:22:19,671
Won't you please decide to donate
for your father's sake?

371
00:22:21,139 --> 00:22:26,478
Never. There's no way I'm giving
my liver to my father.

372
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:28,814
- Yuri--
- Goodbye.

373
00:22:40,225 --> 00:22:44,162
I'm Dr. Ushio, Director of
Next-Generation Intelligent Surgery.

374
00:22:46,798 --> 00:22:49,067
Everyone is afraid of being operated on,

375
00:22:49,167 --> 00:22:51,002
but don't you worry.

376
00:22:51,069 --> 00:22:53,305
I will perform the perfect surgery.

377
00:22:53,905 --> 00:22:58,009
I've conducted over 100 transplants
and have never once failed.

378
00:22:59,277 --> 00:23:01,413
It's not that I'm afraid of surgery.

379
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:06,918
That man is no father.

380
00:23:15,694 --> 00:23:17,262
He's your only father!

381
00:23:19,598 --> 00:23:20,866
Who are you?

382
00:23:21,266 --> 00:23:25,003
Sorry. I'm Dr. Ebina, a surgery staff.

383
00:23:26,338 --> 00:23:29,641
I have a daughter about your age too,

384
00:23:29,708 --> 00:23:31,710
so I shouted without thinking. I'm sorry.

385
00:23:33,712 --> 00:23:37,115
My daughter is in
her rebellious period now.

386
00:23:37,482 --> 00:23:40,886
She says awful things like,
"I hope you die soon, Dad."

387
00:23:41,820 --> 00:23:46,758
But if I really did die,
we couldn't argue.

388
00:23:47,659 --> 00:23:49,094
Wouldn't that be sad?

389
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:52,764
Cut that out.

390
00:23:53,231 --> 00:23:56,601
A doctor demanding a transplant
is unethical.

391
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:03,041
But Yuri...

392
00:24:04,376 --> 00:24:06,745
Everyone wants to save your father.

393
00:24:06,878 --> 00:24:08,547
Will you just cut it out?

394
00:24:19,458 --> 00:24:21,326
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

395
00:24:23,028 --> 00:24:25,864
The Nishiki Group is
a privately-owned company,

396
00:24:25,931 --> 00:24:28,500
but his children want
nothing to do with him?

397
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,369
Since there's nobody to take over
the group,

398
00:24:31,436 --> 00:24:34,339
if the CEO, Toshiro Nishiki, dies,

399
00:24:34,439 --> 00:24:37,375
assets will be drained
through inheritance issues

400
00:24:37,442 --> 00:24:39,344
and the domino effect could cause

401
00:24:39,444 --> 00:24:41,313
dozens of subsidiary companies to fail.

402
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,014
That sounds like trouble.

403
00:24:43,081 --> 00:24:44,649
What does "domino effect" mean?

404
00:24:45,050 --> 00:24:48,987
It means they fall one after
the other like dominoes.

405
00:24:49,054 --> 00:24:50,222
I see.

406
00:24:50,455 --> 00:24:53,325
But no one in his family is willing
to donate their liver, right?

407
00:24:53,391 --> 00:24:57,562
Of course not.
Why would they suffer by giving their

408
00:24:57,729 --> 00:25:01,333
precious liver to that stingy,
arrogant, tormenting father?

409
00:25:01,399 --> 00:25:04,169
If he dies,
then they'll get a huge inheritance.

410
00:25:04,236 --> 00:25:07,639
Even with his money,
none of his family will be his donor.

411
00:25:07,706 --> 00:25:08,840
Now that's misery.

412
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:13,411
Then there's the young man who has love
but no money for surgery.

413
00:25:13,478 --> 00:25:15,881
Who is happier?

414
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:21,019
He has a donor, but there are
stupid problems preventing it.

415
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:23,989
Mi, aren't you going to play today?

416
00:25:25,290 --> 00:25:27,459
Oh, forget about her.
Let's just play, the three of us.

417
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:28,927
You're right. Let's play.

418
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:31,162
Oh, dear!

419
00:25:31,229 --> 00:25:32,931
- What are you doing?
- Hey!

420
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:34,032
Cut that out, would you?

421
00:25:34,099 --> 00:25:36,701
- You messed it all up.
- They're all mixed up.

422
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:39,037
- Why did you go wild at a time like this?
- That's it. Start over.

423
00:25:39,104 --> 00:25:40,672
The domino effect...

424
00:25:54,953 --> 00:25:56,254
Dr. Daimon?

425
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:02,460
Have you also come to tell me
what the other doctors have?

426
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,997
There's no way I'm doing it.

427
00:26:06,464 --> 00:26:09,501
I'm never giving my organs to my father.

428
00:26:11,202 --> 00:26:12,604
That's what I thought.

429
00:26:19,344 --> 00:26:20,445
But

430
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:23,882
you want to save Ken, right?

431
00:26:27,285 --> 00:26:30,589
You'll save Ken?

432
00:26:33,792 --> 00:26:35,393
It depends on how hard you try.

433
00:26:48,306 --> 00:26:51,509
How fucking long do I have to
stay cooped up in here?

434
00:26:51,876 --> 00:26:53,979
Haven't you found a donor yet?

435
00:26:54,245 --> 00:26:57,616
I understand how you feel.
Please be patient for a while longer.

436
00:26:57,749 --> 00:27:00,352
- I know you feel unwell--
- I've had it!

437
00:27:01,252 --> 00:27:03,655
Get out there and buy a liver for me!

438
00:27:04,522 --> 00:27:09,194
I have more than enough money!
I'll pay one billion, even two!

439
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:11,329
Buy me a liver!

440
00:27:12,197 --> 00:27:13,331
Okay.

441
00:27:13,798 --> 00:27:16,167
- How can you say that?
- Dr. Ebina!

442
00:27:16,534 --> 00:27:18,837
- Buy you a liver, right?
- Yes!

443
00:27:20,472 --> 00:27:22,574
You'll be arrested if you do that.

444
00:27:22,707 --> 00:27:24,576
I'm sorry. I can't buy a liver.

445
00:27:25,910 --> 00:27:28,947
- Not you again.
- Dr. Daimon, didn't you know

446
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,983
that this is the private room
of CEO Nishiki?

447
00:27:32,050 --> 00:27:34,719
I brought you a donor.

448
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,799
Yuri?

449
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,504
Yuri! How dare you come here!

450
00:27:54,239 --> 00:27:55,507
Father.

451
00:27:57,175 --> 00:28:02,347
I didn't know about your disease.

452
00:28:05,684 --> 00:28:07,852
I know you never told Mom or my brothers

453
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:10,922
and suffered all by yourself. Right?

454
00:28:12,991 --> 00:28:16,094
I'm sorry I never noticed.

455
00:28:19,631 --> 00:28:22,467
Yuri's the only one
who would give her liver

456
00:28:23,001 --> 00:28:25,270
to a father like you, right?

457
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:29,874
You're just after my money, aren't you?

458
00:28:29,941 --> 00:28:32,010
I bet that you went broke
hanging out with that guy.

459
00:28:32,077 --> 00:28:35,213
How much do you want?
One hundred million? One billion?

460
00:28:36,081 --> 00:28:37,716
I don't want any stupid money.

461
00:28:38,917 --> 00:28:41,686
I want you to get well, Father.

462
00:28:47,959 --> 00:28:49,194
Yuri...

463
00:28:54,299 --> 00:28:57,869
Daimon, I didn't think you had it in you.

464
00:28:59,637 --> 00:29:02,173
There is an eighty-percent
survival rate after five years

465
00:29:02,507 --> 00:29:04,209
for living-donor liver transplants.

466
00:29:04,609 --> 00:29:08,146
There's a 15-percent rate
of complications.

467
00:29:08,213 --> 00:29:11,850
That means this is a difficult
surgery that carries risks.

468
00:29:12,617 --> 00:29:14,018
If there are any mistakes,

469
00:29:14,119 --> 00:29:18,156
even though you're healthy,
you could lose your own life.

470
00:29:19,457 --> 00:29:21,092
Shouldn't you reconsider?

471
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:23,661
Yuri.

472
00:29:24,596 --> 00:29:26,030
Are you sure?

473
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,571
Dr. Daimon.

474
00:29:39,511 --> 00:29:42,580
I never fail.

475
00:29:46,217 --> 00:29:47,652
Please take care of this.

476
00:29:57,228 --> 00:30:00,465
Regarding Toshiro Nishiki's
living-donor liver transplant,

477
00:30:00,532 --> 00:30:04,569
the donor is his daughter,
Yuri Nishiki, age 23.

478
00:30:05,103 --> 00:30:07,906
Her blood type is compatible,
and her liver function is normal.

479
00:30:07,972 --> 00:30:10,208
HLA typing is also not a problem.

480
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:13,144
- The surgeon--
- Me!

481
00:30:13,344 --> 00:30:15,313
- Me!
- Me!

482
00:30:17,148 --> 00:30:20,852
I have done over 100
live liver transplants in the US.

483
00:30:21,052 --> 00:30:23,555
This is an extremely important operation,

484
00:30:23,788 --> 00:30:26,958
so as Director of Next-Generation
Intelligent Surgery, I should do it.

485
00:30:27,025 --> 00:30:31,162
No. As Director of Next-Generation
Ultra-Minimally Invasive Surgery,

486
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:33,264
I should do it.

487
00:30:34,399 --> 00:30:36,467
I'm the one who got the donor.

488
00:30:39,604 --> 00:30:43,107
- Everyone really wants to do this.
- They all think it's attractive.

489
00:30:43,374 --> 00:30:46,144
The Nishiki Group is rolling in money.

490
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:47,879
- So it's for money.
- Right.

491
00:30:48,112 --> 00:30:51,616
Nichotan!

492
00:30:53,117 --> 00:30:54,819
Definitely not her.

493
00:30:55,553 --> 00:30:56,855
Like her surgery the other day,

494
00:30:56,921 --> 00:31:00,425
uncontrollable doctors outside
the AI's predictions are dangerous.

495
00:31:01,693 --> 00:31:04,462
She's very talented, but you're right.

496
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:15,740
For the organ removal surgery
on the donor...

497
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:25,783
- I'd like you to do it, Dr. Kaji.
- Yes, sir.

498
00:31:27,185 --> 00:31:30,188
For the transplant surgery
on Toshiro Nishiki...

499
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:42,100
Dr. Ushio, the fate of
Totei rests on this surgery.

500
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:46,004
- Cooperate with Dr. Kaji on this.
- Yes, sir.

501
00:31:59,651 --> 00:32:02,720
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

502
00:32:11,629 --> 00:32:14,933
We will now conduct Yuri Nishiki's
donor surgery.

503
00:32:15,033 --> 00:32:17,101
- Let us begin.
- Yes, sir.

504
00:32:17,168 --> 00:32:18,336
- Scalpel.
- Here.

505
00:32:31,683 --> 00:32:32,517
<i>Here.</i>

506
00:32:41,492 --> 00:32:43,161
OPERATING ROOM 2
TOSHIRO NISHIKI

507
00:32:49,233 --> 00:32:50,768
Abdominal opening is complete.

508
00:32:52,537 --> 00:32:55,673
<i>Resect the falciform ligament
of the liver.</i>

509
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:58,309
Here.

510
00:33:07,452 --> 00:33:09,554
Resection of the falciform ligament
of the liver is complete.

511
00:33:10,488 --> 00:33:13,157
<i>Use the liver retractor to
widen the surgical view.</i>

512
00:33:13,524 --> 00:33:15,727
<i>Detach the porta hepatis.</i>

513
00:33:27,205 --> 00:33:30,308
SURGERY TIME

514
00:33:32,877 --> 00:33:36,347
Portal vein taping is complete.
Let's elevate the right liver.

515
00:33:41,819 --> 00:33:43,755
The liver is more swollen than expected.

516
00:33:44,022 --> 00:33:47,058
This will make handling of
the short hepatic vein tough.

517
00:33:47,158 --> 00:33:51,496
<i>Detach and move the liver from
the retroperitoneum.</i>

518
00:33:53,998 --> 00:33:55,600
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

519
00:34:01,973 --> 00:34:03,674
Detaching left hepatic vein.

520
00:34:03,741 --> 00:34:05,043
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

521
00:34:05,209 --> 00:34:07,879
YURI NISHIKI

522
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,915
LEFT LIVER LOBE REMOVAL
LEFT LOBE OF THE LIVER

523
00:34:10,982 --> 00:34:12,784
Removal of left liver lobe is complete.

524
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:15,520
Ice the graft
and fill it with the preservation agent.

525
00:34:16,587 --> 00:34:17,922
- Gauze.
- Here.

526
00:34:20,858 --> 00:34:23,061
We'll shape the hepatic vein
with a clip-graft.

527
00:34:23,127 --> 00:34:24,495
- Drop my loupe.
- Yes, sir.

528
00:34:25,696 --> 00:34:27,465
- 6-0 monofilament.
- Here.

529
00:34:34,172 --> 00:34:35,540
I'll stop the hemorrhaging now.

530
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:36,974
Here.

531
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:45,016
<i>The left lobe graft has been completed
in operating room one.</i>

532
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:47,819
<i>Remove the liver within 30 minutes</i>

533
00:34:47,885 --> 00:34:51,022
<i>and prepare the patient
for receiving the graft.</i>

534
00:34:55,293 --> 00:34:56,360
Dr. Ushio.

535
00:34:59,097 --> 00:35:01,232
Separating ligature
from short hepatic vein.

536
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:03,134
- 4-0 absorbable suture.
- Here.

537
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:06,737
<i>Handling of the short hepatic vein
is very important.</i>

538
00:35:07,038 --> 00:35:10,074
<i>Please detach it carefully.</i>

539
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,718
<i>Shaping is complete. Okay.</i>

540
00:35:21,252 --> 00:35:23,955
<i>- Take the graft to operating room two.
- Yes.</i>

541
00:35:24,355 --> 00:35:28,926
The liver graft is being taken
from operating room two to one.

542
00:35:28,993 --> 00:35:31,796
It's progressing nicely so far.

543
00:35:44,575 --> 00:35:46,077
I've brought the graft.

544
00:35:46,344 --> 00:35:49,113
TOSHIRO NISHIKI

545
00:35:49,180 --> 00:35:51,449
We'll soon be finished with
removing the liver here.

546
00:35:51,516 --> 00:35:52,583
LIVER EXCISION

547
00:35:58,022 --> 00:36:02,160
<i>Please proceed with
vein detachment carefully.</i>

548
00:36:07,899 --> 00:36:11,636
Are you sure it's okay?
BP has fallen below 70!

549
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:16,174
Inferior vena cava has been damaged.

550
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:18,075
<i>Surgery falling behind schedule.</i>

551
00:36:18,476 --> 00:36:21,012
<i>Please hurry to complete
removal of the liver.</i>

552
00:36:21,078 --> 00:36:23,181
It's fine!

553
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,550
I can't suction fast enough!

554
00:36:25,716 --> 00:36:27,652
Hemorrhaging has exceeded 1,000.

555
00:36:29,153 --> 00:36:30,855
- Suction properly!
- Sorry!

556
00:36:33,791 --> 00:36:35,393
Things are not okay.

557
00:36:36,394 --> 00:36:39,430
At this rate,
other blood vessels will become damaged.

558
00:36:39,530 --> 00:36:41,499
There's a risk of a domino effect.

559
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:44,969
<i>- Stop the hemorrhaging!
- It's fine!</i>

560
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:46,771
<i>Follow the AI's instructions.</i>

561
00:36:50,641 --> 00:36:53,544
<i>Stay calm. What are the AI's instructions?</i>

562
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:58,849
<i>The weight of the left lobe graft
is lower than expected.</i>

563
00:36:59,417 --> 00:37:02,787
<i>It's below 30 percent of
the necessary weight.</i>

564
00:37:03,254 --> 00:37:07,692
<i>There is a possibility of post-op
small-for-size graft syndrome.</i>

565
00:37:09,794 --> 00:37:13,497
- Then what should I do?
<i>- Cancel the transplant</i>

566
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:16,734
<i>and end the operation
after stopping the hemorrhaging.</i>

567
00:37:16,801 --> 00:37:18,636
- What?
- Are you kidding?

568
00:37:18,703 --> 00:37:20,271
You can't disobey the AI.

569
00:37:21,973 --> 00:37:23,407
- Gauze!
- Here.

570
00:37:27,478 --> 00:37:29,046
I can't believe this.

571
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:33,918
What'll happen to his investment to
the Totei University Hospital fund?

572
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:35,953
That's one billion yen!

573
00:37:37,822 --> 00:37:40,558
If this fails,
we'll lose one billion in investment!

574
00:37:41,492 --> 00:37:42,827
Are you kidding?

575
00:37:43,294 --> 00:37:44,295
Get out of there!

576
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,064
<i>- Gauze.
- Here.</i>

577
00:37:47,131 --> 00:37:50,268
Dr. Ushio! Don't give up! Hang in there!

578
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:54,005
If this operation fails,
it will cost us one billion yen!

579
00:37:54,071 --> 00:37:55,306
<i>One billion!</i>

580
00:38:00,077 --> 00:38:03,147
Like the AI has instructed,
we're ending this operation.

581
00:38:05,349 --> 00:38:07,351
- Yes, sir.
- Hold on!

582
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:09,487
What about the donor?

583
00:38:09,553 --> 00:38:11,922
His daughter's liver has
already been removed!

584
00:38:13,391 --> 00:38:14,759
- Gauze.
- Here.

585
00:38:15,426 --> 00:38:17,995
- Suture.
- Here.

586
00:38:39,216 --> 00:38:40,351
Michiko Daimon!

587
00:38:40,418 --> 00:38:41,552
<i>Out of the way.</i>

588
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:47,091
Oh, dear! Look at all the damage
to the blood vessels!

589
00:38:47,158 --> 00:38:49,527
Was this also the instructions of the AI?

590
00:38:50,428 --> 00:38:53,631
<i>End the surgery.</i>

591
00:38:53,731 --> 00:38:54,965
Shut up!

592
00:38:55,032 --> 00:38:56,400
- Turn off the sound.
- Right.

593
00:38:56,467 --> 00:38:59,203
<i>End the surgery...</i>

594
00:39:03,507 --> 00:39:04,642
Adding procedure.

595
00:39:04,742 --> 00:39:07,912
Adding portal vein and IVC shunt
for small-for-size graft.

596
00:39:08,079 --> 00:39:10,948
For vessel damage, I'll block the IVC
to stop the hemorrhaging.

597
00:39:11,882 --> 00:39:13,284
- Prepare crushed ice.
- Right.

598
00:39:13,884 --> 00:39:14,719
Here.

599
00:39:20,091 --> 00:39:22,226
Why are you just standing there?
Open the surgical field.

600
00:39:22,493 --> 00:39:24,161
- 4-0 absorbable suture.
- Here.

601
00:39:36,173 --> 00:39:39,009
She'll transfer blood flow from
the portal vein to the IVC

602
00:39:39,276 --> 00:39:41,579
by creating a new pathway.

603
00:39:41,846 --> 00:39:43,714
That will keep the portal blood pressure
under control

604
00:39:44,081 --> 00:39:46,550
and increase blood flow
in the hepatic artery.

605
00:39:47,451 --> 00:39:50,855
You mean it makes a small-for-size
liver transplant possible?

606
00:39:58,462 --> 00:40:03,267
Portal vein and IVC shunt prep
and liver removal, complete.

607
00:40:03,968 --> 00:40:07,037
I'm putting in the graft.
Give me the left lobe graft.

608
00:40:21,118 --> 00:40:23,888
SURGERY TIME

609
00:40:25,055 --> 00:40:26,223
Finished.

610
00:40:41,739 --> 00:40:42,840
Hey!

611
00:40:43,874 --> 00:40:46,444
- What is Dr. Daimon doing?
<i>- You kept it clean and cool, right?</i>

612
00:40:47,077 --> 00:40:48,279
<i>Yes.</i>

613
00:40:54,385 --> 00:40:56,687
- I'm taking this.
- You're taking it?

614
00:40:59,256 --> 00:41:02,493
What's going on? What was that about?

615
00:41:03,194 --> 00:41:05,930
That's the liver that was removed
from this patient, right?

616
00:41:08,065 --> 00:41:10,734
Anyway, I'm sure it doesn't matter.

617
00:41:11,001 --> 00:41:12,803
Where the heck did she take it?

618
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:16,040
She's entered this operating room.

619
00:41:17,942 --> 00:41:21,078
- Did it go well?
- Yes, but it took some work.

620
00:41:22,413 --> 00:41:23,681
Sorry I kept you waiting.

621
00:41:23,814 --> 00:41:28,519
His BP is 127 over 82. Pulse, 78.

622
00:41:28,586 --> 00:41:29,720
Let's begin.

623
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:30,721
We will now conduct

624
00:41:30,788 --> 00:41:34,391
a living-donor liver transplant
from Toshiro Nishiki to Kenji Kosawa.

625
00:41:34,925 --> 00:41:36,126
- Scalpel.
- Here.

626
00:41:42,266 --> 00:41:43,701
What the heck is going on here?

627
00:41:45,102 --> 00:41:47,872
Yuri Nishiki became a donor

628
00:41:48,105 --> 00:41:51,408
to save her beloved boyfriend as well.

629
00:41:52,042 --> 00:41:53,344
What?

630
00:41:58,048 --> 00:42:00,351
TRANSPLANT AGREEMENT
FIRST RECEIPT

631
00:42:03,120 --> 00:42:04,255
NISHIKI

632
00:42:04,588 --> 00:42:08,759
Father, I have one request.

633
00:42:09,894 --> 00:42:13,964
What is it? If you want money,
I'll give you as much as you like.

634
00:42:14,398 --> 00:42:15,533
That's not what I want.

635
00:42:22,907 --> 00:42:25,309
Can you sign this as well?

636
00:42:27,645 --> 00:42:32,416
It's an agreement to use the liver
removed from you in another patient.

637
00:42:32,750 --> 00:42:33,884
What's this all about?

638
00:42:35,252 --> 00:42:38,455
Please, Father. I want you to save him.

639
00:42:42,593 --> 00:42:44,094
This is for him?

640
00:42:44,495 --> 00:42:47,665
<i>That was an agreement to allow the use of</i>

641
00:42:47,865 --> 00:42:53,203
<i>her father's liver
in an urgent necessity for a third party.</i>

642
00:42:54,204 --> 00:42:58,042
Transplants from a first recipient
to a second recipient

643
00:42:58,943 --> 00:43:04,081
can be approved when done
for a non-relative third party.

644
00:43:05,215 --> 00:43:08,619
By doing this, Yuri donated
her liver to her father

645
00:43:09,486 --> 00:43:15,659
and her father donated his liver
to Yuri's boyfriend.

646
00:43:19,763 --> 00:43:25,035
It's called the living-donor
domino liver transplant.

647
00:43:30,474 --> 00:43:31,942
- Sealing device.
- Here.

648
00:43:41,852 --> 00:43:45,422
SURGERY TIME

649
00:43:50,694 --> 00:43:51,862
Okay. Finished.

650
00:44:01,572 --> 00:44:05,242
Dr. Daimon, thank you for saving Kosawa.

651
00:44:05,576 --> 00:44:06,910
You too, Tako.

652
00:44:07,511 --> 00:44:08,812
Thank you!

653
00:44:36,407 --> 00:44:37,641
Hey, Ebi.

654
00:44:39,176 --> 00:44:42,880
You know, I understand how he feels.

655
00:44:43,280 --> 00:44:44,314
What?

656
00:44:45,015 --> 00:44:46,050
Can you take this?

657
00:44:46,717 --> 00:44:49,353
Hey, don't do it. Ebi!

658
00:44:53,190 --> 00:44:56,627
Excuse me, I may be butting in,

659
00:44:57,194 --> 00:44:59,029
but everyone gets depressed
about it at first.

660
00:45:00,564 --> 00:45:03,667
You're not the only one who's been
overcome by a sense of defeat.

661
00:45:04,568 --> 00:45:07,805
Michiko Daimon isn't an ordinary doctor,
so it can't be helped.

662
00:45:10,107 --> 00:45:13,210
Change and challenge!

663
00:45:14,344 --> 00:45:17,314
If you'd like,
I'll join you for a drink tonight.

664
00:45:17,748 --> 00:45:18,849
We'll go Dutch.

665
00:45:20,451 --> 00:45:23,554
You're a plebe, right?

666
00:45:26,056 --> 00:45:28,959
Oh, that's right. Sorry. I'm a plebe.

667
00:45:29,093 --> 00:45:30,327
Sorry, I stepped out of line.

668
00:45:35,666 --> 00:45:39,002
I keep on forgetting that I'm a plebe.

669
00:45:39,103 --> 00:45:41,405
I just can't seem to
get used to being a plebe.

670
00:45:41,472 --> 00:45:44,108
You did good. That was impressive.

671
00:46:00,791 --> 00:46:02,259
How is Ken?

672
00:46:03,894 --> 00:46:07,631
He's still asleep under anesthesia,
but he's fine now.

673
00:46:09,767 --> 00:46:12,770
Your father's liver was very weak,

674
00:46:13,437 --> 00:46:15,973
but it was good
to donate to your boyfriend.

675
00:46:18,308 --> 00:46:22,713
Dr. Daimon, thank you for everything.

676
00:46:24,214 --> 00:46:26,517
I never fail.

677
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:31,388
You're pretty amazing.

678
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:33,724
You got her to be a donor
for her wealthy father

679
00:46:33,957 --> 00:46:36,160
and even got him to approve your marriage.

680
00:46:37,761 --> 00:46:39,963
It's all thanks to Dr. Daimon.

681
00:46:40,531 --> 00:46:45,369
All I did was operate. Leave
the troublesome talk like that to Tako.

682
00:46:46,236 --> 00:46:47,871
There she goes again.

683
00:46:56,580 --> 00:46:58,549
I'm starving!

684
00:47:00,317 --> 00:47:02,219
Akira!

685
00:47:02,686 --> 00:47:06,423
As a reward for the great operation,
I'll buy you <i>takoyaki</i>!

686
00:47:07,424 --> 00:47:10,093
I'm so happy! But I'm...

687
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:13,530
- What is it?
- Forget it.

688
00:47:13,730 --> 00:47:15,332
Okay, let's go!

689
00:47:15,799 --> 00:47:17,968
- Two, please!
- Welcome. Go ahead. Take two.

690
00:47:18,068 --> 00:47:20,671
- Okay. Which should I take?
- Here you are. Thank you.

691
00:47:20,771 --> 00:47:22,439
- It's hot!
- Thank you.

692
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:25,976
This is awesome!

693
00:47:26,276 --> 00:47:28,278
Okay, let's eat.

694
00:47:28,378 --> 00:47:30,881
This looks delicious!

695
00:47:31,348 --> 00:47:32,983
Here I go.

696
00:47:33,083 --> 00:47:34,618
Hold on.

697
00:47:40,490 --> 00:47:43,894
- This seems awfully big.
- Was there octopus in mine?

698
00:47:43,961 --> 00:47:45,229
The octopus is big.

699
00:47:45,996 --> 00:47:49,166
- Yours are bigger than mine!
- Not true. They're the same.

700
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:50,667
We concluded a contract

701
00:47:50,767 --> 00:47:53,403
for one billion in investment
from the Nishiki Group.

702
00:47:53,871 --> 00:47:57,975
How is the Totei University Hospital
Rebirth Plan 2020 going?

703
00:47:58,208 --> 00:48:01,144
Just as planned,
funds will be garnered from

704
00:48:01,278 --> 00:48:03,814
the redevelopment
of the closed Lake Mashu,

705
00:48:03,881 --> 00:48:07,317
Oga, and Kusatsu hospitals
which will be turned into

706
00:48:07,451 --> 00:48:09,519
resort condos for Chinese and Australians.

707
00:48:09,720 --> 00:48:13,724
It's still not enough. What other
satellite hospitals can be closed?

708
00:48:13,790 --> 00:48:17,694
Within six months, five other
satellite hospitals can be closed.

709
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:20,564
Okutama Satellite Hospital 17,

710
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:24,534
Yonaguni Satellite Hospital 5,
Wajima Satellite Hospital 10,

711
00:48:24,735 --> 00:48:26,970
Ibigawa Satellite Hospital 12,

712
00:48:27,070 --> 00:48:29,439
Genkai Sea Satellite Hospital 20.

713
00:48:30,207 --> 00:48:34,077
We can garner 20 billion
in redevelopment funds from these.

714
00:48:36,613 --> 00:48:40,250
Acting Director, Mr. Kanbara is here
from the Famous Doctor Agency.

715
00:48:48,325 --> 00:48:49,760
Acting Hospital Director,

716
00:48:50,460 --> 00:48:55,032
I'm glad to hear your cost cutting
is snipping along smoothly.

717
00:48:56,099 --> 00:48:57,301
This is a melon.

718
00:48:59,836 --> 00:49:01,305
This is the bill.

719
00:49:04,408 --> 00:49:06,076
PLEASE PAY THE FOLLOWING AMOUNT

720
00:49:07,678 --> 00:49:10,547
In this era? You must be kidding.

721
00:49:10,747 --> 00:49:14,685
Also, Acting Hospital Director Tange
just had melon

722
00:49:14,785 --> 00:49:16,520
for dessert during breakfast.

723
00:49:16,987 --> 00:49:19,556
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

724
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:25,195
Then would you please give it
to Director Hiruma in jail?

725
00:49:25,462 --> 00:49:27,965
I don't know who leaked his deeds
to the police,

726
00:49:28,365 --> 00:49:33,036
but I heard he's become worn out
from the harsh daily interrogations.

727
00:49:34,237 --> 00:49:38,742
Melons are Director Hiruma's favorite.

728
00:49:40,043 --> 00:49:41,411
I see.

729
00:49:41,878 --> 00:49:47,551
The great deed of Japan's first AI-guided

730
00:49:47,751 --> 00:49:52,489
living-donor liver transplant
conducted by Michiko Daimon

731
00:49:53,090 --> 00:49:57,828
will be credited entirely to
Director Ushio.

732
00:49:58,662 --> 00:50:02,632
Considering the remuneration, donation,

733
00:50:02,733 --> 00:50:07,037
and investment of significant funds
in the reconstruction plan,

734
00:50:08,305 --> 00:50:10,774
this is quite inexpensive.

735
00:50:17,114 --> 00:50:19,549
I never give a discount for my price.

736
00:50:31,061 --> 00:50:37,034
Thank you, Nichotan!

737
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:43,573
Yes! Nichotan!

738
00:50:43,640 --> 00:50:46,743
ONE MONTH LATER

739
00:50:47,411 --> 00:50:51,114
- Congratulations on your release.
- Thank you.

740
00:50:51,748 --> 00:50:53,917
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

741
00:50:55,118 --> 00:50:58,588
Dr. Tako, everyone,
thank you for your help.

742
00:50:59,356 --> 00:51:01,525
I'm glad you got your surgery!

743
00:51:02,259 --> 00:51:06,129
The liver you received may
develop amyloidosis in the future,

744
00:51:06,263 --> 00:51:09,266
but it has given you a new lease on life,
so treat it well.

745
00:51:11,168 --> 00:51:13,437
I have one other announcement.

746
00:51:15,038 --> 00:51:17,274
We're going to the city office after this.

747
00:51:22,279 --> 00:51:24,881
We're going to get married.

748
00:51:24,948 --> 00:51:27,884
Really? Now?

749
00:51:27,951 --> 00:51:30,120
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

750
00:51:30,287 --> 00:51:31,888
That's great!

751
00:51:32,055 --> 00:51:34,291
- Checkmate!
- Right, checkmate.

752
00:51:34,357 --> 00:51:35,992
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

753
00:51:36,126 --> 00:51:38,061
This really is great.

754
00:51:39,996 --> 00:51:41,331
What's this?

755
00:51:42,299 --> 00:51:46,870
I didn't know you could feel joy
at someone else's happiness.

756
00:51:47,003 --> 00:51:51,842
They'll marry, have children,
and their liver can be transplanted.

757
00:51:52,309 --> 00:51:54,744
A salvage living-donor liver transplant.

758
00:51:54,845 --> 00:51:59,216
When I think about doing that,
I get so excited!

759
00:52:03,186 --> 00:52:05,222
All she wants is to do surgery.

760
00:52:05,288 --> 00:52:07,791
- Congratulations.
- I'm so happy for you.

761
00:52:17,434 --> 00:52:18,768
Dr. Michiko Daimon,

762
00:52:18,935 --> 00:52:21,505
your living-donor domino
liver transplant was magnificent.

763
00:52:21,738 --> 00:52:24,341
- I'm glad it succeeded.
- I'm very pleased.

764
00:52:25,142 --> 00:52:29,513
You are truly a goddess
who never makes mistakes.

765
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:35,352
I'm glad you were able to save
that wealthy patient.

766
00:52:45,695 --> 00:52:48,064
Congratulations on your release.

767
00:52:48,932 --> 00:52:50,200
Congratulations.

768
00:52:54,971 --> 00:52:56,873
And thank you for your donation.

769
00:52:57,340 --> 00:52:58,241
You!

770
00:52:59,409 --> 00:53:02,045
- You're a pretty darn good surgeon.
- Thank you.

771
00:53:02,512 --> 00:53:06,283
The scar is hardly noticeable. I like you!

772
00:53:06,383 --> 00:53:07,484
Thank you.

773
00:53:07,584 --> 00:53:09,486
I'll call on you again
if anything else happens.

774
00:53:09,553 --> 00:53:10,387
Yes.

775
00:53:10,453 --> 00:53:12,489
- We'll be ready for you.
- Good!

776
00:53:23,833 --> 00:53:27,871
Now you can publish a paper
about the AI-guided

777
00:53:28,138 --> 00:53:31,675
- living-donor liver transplant.
- Right.

778
00:53:39,849 --> 00:53:42,552
- "Right"? Give me a break!
- You know,

779
00:53:42,619 --> 00:53:45,021
Director Ushio was getting a lot of
compliments today. How come?

780
00:53:45,088 --> 00:53:47,424
He messed up that surgery!

781
00:53:47,490 --> 00:53:50,393
That's right. If Dr. Daimon hadn't
covered for his mistakes,

782
00:53:50,594 --> 00:53:53,964
he wouldn't be close to release.
There'd be huge trouble.

783
00:53:54,130 --> 00:53:55,999
- That's so right.
- That's so right.

784
00:53:57,000 --> 00:53:59,469
But in an organization like this,

785
00:53:59,569 --> 00:54:01,571
it's guys like that who get promoted.

786
00:54:02,606 --> 00:54:03,974
I wonder how Director Hiruma is doing.

787
00:54:04,274 --> 00:54:06,376
Come to think of it,
you got a huge remuneration, right?

788
00:54:09,813 --> 00:54:11,648
I completely forgot

789
00:54:12,182 --> 00:54:14,084
what I had done!

790
00:54:14,517 --> 00:54:16,720
I forgot!

791
00:54:29,399 --> 00:54:32,068
- Watch out!
- I'm going to fall!

792
00:54:32,168 --> 00:54:34,271
- Hold on!
- Help!

793
00:54:39,109 --> 00:54:41,144
- Be careful.
- You can do it!

794
00:54:41,311 --> 00:54:43,079
- You can do it!
- I'm scared!

795
00:54:43,313 --> 00:54:46,249
- You can do it!
- You can do it!

796
00:55:00,063 --> 00:55:02,899
<i>She hates groups, hates authority,</i>

797
00:55:03,366 --> 00:55:04,801
<i>- and hates restrictions.</i>
- Okay, everyone!

798
00:55:05,201 --> 00:55:07,270
- Here goes!
<i>- Her specialized medical license</i>

799
00:55:07,370 --> 00:55:10,507
- <i>and well-honed skills are her weapons.</i>
- Okay!

800
00:55:10,607 --> 00:55:11,908
Ready. Go!

801
00:55:12,876 --> 00:55:14,878
- Go!
- Go!

802
00:55:15,378 --> 00:55:16,379
Go!

803
00:55:41,905 --> 00:55:42,806
We did it!

804
00:55:42,872 --> 00:55:45,642
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

805
00:55:45,742 --> 00:55:49,079
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

806
00:57:15,632 --> 00:57:17,667
Good afternoon, common folk!

807
00:57:17,734 --> 00:57:18,568
<i>Are you stupid?</i>

808
00:57:18,635 --> 00:57:20,637
Gossip shows never tire of scandal.

809
00:57:20,703 --> 00:57:22,639
<i>The gaffe-prone minister
has tongue cancer.</i>

810
00:57:23,673 --> 00:57:24,941
<i>I have the final decision!</i>

811
00:57:25,008 --> 00:57:27,844
In this world, this is called
"reading between the lines."

812
00:57:27,944 --> 00:57:29,913
I never make gaffes.
